om/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 13 Game Day Kickoff: Nothing compares to the outright hatred of a rival","description":"What to expect in Rivalry Week, from top games and players to teams on upset alert.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff112526/week-13-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Oklahoma State extends Morris with new 6-year deal","description":"Oklahoma State and head coach Eric Morris have agreed to a new six-year deal that will extend his contract through the 2032 season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T17:00:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50594432/sources-oklahoma-state-extends-morris-new-six-year-deal","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Where is 'College GameDay'? 2026 schedule, locations, recaps","description":"What is the \"College GameDay\" schedule? Find out more about where the program will be each week of the 2026 college football season.","published":"2026-11-25T15:16:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49783645/where-college-gameday-2026-schedule-locations-recaps","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922988/jamari-johnson","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Johnson"},"pick":{"pick":24,"round":1,"team":"CIN","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jamari Johnson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Johnson","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"Jamari Johnson is an American college football tight end for the Oregon Ducks. He previously played for the Louisville Cardinals.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Johnson attended Inglewood High School in Inglewood, California. He originally played quarterback before switching to tight end and also played wide receiver, running back and defensive end. As a senior, he was named the Ocean League MVP. Johnson was selected to play in the 2023 All-American Bowl. He committed to the University of Louisville to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Johnson played in five games and redshirted his first year at Louisville in 2023. He played in seven games as a redshirt freshman in 2024, recording 13 receptions for 158 yards and a touchdown, before suffering a season ending ankle injury. After the season, he entered the transfer portal and transferred to the University of Oregon. Johnson spent his first season at Oregon in 2025 as the backup to Kenyon Sadiq."}]}}